  "question": {
    "text": "In a hypothetical fission reaction\n${ }_{92} X^{236} \\rightarrow{ }_{56} Y^{141}+{ }_{36} Z^{92}+3 R$\nThe identity of emitted particles ( $\\mathrm{R})$ is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "L1jwn",
      "text": "Electron",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "f5pIF",
      "text": "Neutron",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "pAJqx",
      "text": "$\\gamma$-radiations",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "m32s5",
      "text": "Proton",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{Z} \\text { in LHS }=92 \\\\\n& \\mathrm{Z} \\text { in } \\mathrm{RHS}=56+36=92 \\\\\n& \\mathrm{~A} \\text { in } \\mathrm{LHS}=236 \\\\\n& \\mathrm{~A} \\text { in } \\mathrm{RHS}=141+92=233\n\\end{aligned}$<br />So 3 neutrons are released.",
